    "noteId": "6a797a930000000002003c00",
    "title": "Meet LOTUS OMNI.",
    "desc": "I spent the last 9 months doing something most people say can't be done alone:\nI designed a complete superscalar out-of-order RISC-V processor — with an AI\ntensor accelerator — from scratch, and timing-closed it on real FPGA.\n\t\nMeet LOTUS OMNI.\n\t\nWhat I built (solo):\n• 4-wide OoO RV64I core — TAGE branch prediction, checkpointed register\nrenaming, partitioned reservation stations, 32-entry ROB, 128-entry PRF\n• Dual 8×8 systolic tensor arrays (BF16 + INT8) with 2:4 structured sparsity\n• 3-level cache hierarchy + stride prefetcher\n• 2-D mesh NoC with credit-based congestion control\n\t\nThe proof (Xilinx Vivado, post-route):\n✅ Timing MET @ 80 MHz — WNS +0.141 ns, 0 failing endpoints\n✅ Tensor 8×8 MATMUL verified 64/64 in self-checking simulation\n✅ 55k LUT / 38k FF / 17 BRAM / 64 DSP — zero latches\n✅ Timing closure from −7.019 ns → +0.141 ns\n\t\nI'm self-taught. No team, no shortcuts — just curiosity, discipline, and\nthousands of hours of RTL. Everything is open-source, with full documentation\nand raw Vivado reports:\n\t\n🔗 https://github.com/Sanuka-cmd-net/lotus-omni\n\t\nI'm looking for internships and junior RTL / digital-design roles where I can\nkeep building real silicon. If you're hiring — or know someone who is —\nI'd love to talk.\n\t\n#viral[话题]# #rtl[话题]# #vlsi[话题]# #computer葛[话题]# #hardware[话题]# #opensource[话题]# #semiconductors[话题]# #china[话题]# #fulltime[话题]# #folowers[话题]#",
